---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Kaine Cohen — CohenHolmes"
  description="Who's behind CohenHolmes — a Microsoft security and identity consultant moving into AI engineering, and the tools and writing built along the way."
  canonicalPath="/about"
>
  <meta slot="head" http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'">

  <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
  <h1>The person behind CohenHolmes</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Not a CV — that's what LinkedIn is for. Just who I actually am.
  </p>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Who I am</h2>
    <p>
      I'm Kaine, a Microsoft security and identity consultant based in the UK. Eight years in
      enterprise IT, five of them in identity, across 20+ client environments.
    </p>
    <p>
      I find technology fascinating well beyond the day job. How you secure an application, how
      you run an environment properly, and how all of that has to adapt as AI reshapes the
      processes underneath: that's what I think about, in and out of work.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>How I work with AI</h2>
    <p>
      I use AI as far more than a chat assistant. It drafts the first version of a solution,
      wires systems together, and does real work inside real processes.
    </p>
    <p>
      I treat it as a working partner. I scope the problem, push back on what comes out,
      iterate, and keep the judgement for myself. This site, and everything on it, was built
      that way.
    </p>
    <p>
      My background is identity and security, and that shapes how I see AI. Once agents can
      read data and take actions, the questions that matter are the ones I've spent years on:
      who or what is acting, with which permissions, on which data, and who is accountable.
      Identity becomes the control plane for AI as much as for people.
    </p>
    <p>
      So the move into AI engineering and architecture is a natural extension of the work. I
      want to help organisations adopt AI securely and with proper governance, so it's useful
      from day one.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>What I've built</h2>
    <p>
      The same instinct each time: build the thing I wanted to exist while I was working
      something out myself.
    </p>
    <div class="grid">
      <a class="card" href="/ca-builder">
        <div class="kicker">Tooling</div>
        <p>An interactive Conditional Access Policy Builder — plain-English input, live Microsoft Graph-style JSON out.</p>
        <span class="more">Open the builder →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/ai-governance-check">
        <div class="kicker">AI Governance</div>
        <p>A private, browser-only readiness check across data, identity, governance, agents and human oversight.</p>
        <span class="more">Check your readiness →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/mcp">
        <div class="kicker">For agents</div>
        <p>A read-only MCP server exposing this blog to any AI agent — list posts, fetch the latest, read one in full.</p>
        <span class="more">Connect your agent →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/blog">
        <div class="kicker">Writing</div>
        <p>Notes on identity, security and the move into AI engineering — usually working something out in public.</p>
        <span class="more">Read the blog →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="contact">
    <h2>Say hello</h2>
    <p>
      Happy to talk identity, security, compliance, or where AI fits into any of them — or about
      any of the above.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="https://linkedin.com/in/kainecohen" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn ↗</a>
      <a class="button" href="mailto:kaine.cohen@cohenholmes.co.uk">Email</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .eyebrow{
    margin:0 0 16px;
    font-family:var(--font-mono);
    font-size:0.76rem;
    letter-spacing:0.12em;
    text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--accent-text);
  }
  .lede{
    max-width:70ch;
    margin-top:18px;
    font-size:clamp(1.02rem, 1.6vw, 1.18rem);
    color:#4A4A5A;
  }

  .block{ margin-top:56px; }
  .block > p{ max-width:68ch; }

  .grid{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap:18px;
    margin-top:22px;
  }
  .card{
    background:#FCFAF6;
    border:1px solid #E3DFD3;
    border-radius:16px;
    padding:22px 20px;
    box-shadow:0 8px 18px rgba(15,30,51,0.06);
    text-decoration:none;
    transition:transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .card:hover{ transform:translateY(-2px); border-color:var(--accent); }
  .card:focus-visible{ outline:2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset:2px; }
  .card .kicker{
    font-family:var(--font-body);
    color:var(--accent-text);
    font-weight:500;
    font-size:0.72rem;
    letter-spacing:0.11em;
    text-transform:uppercase;
    margin-bottom:10px;
  }
  .card p{ margin:0; color:#4A4A5A; font-size:0.95rem; }
  .card .more{
    display:inline-block;
    margin-top:10px;
    font-size:0.85rem;
    color:var(--navy);
  }

  .actions{
    display:flex;
    flex-wrap:wrap;
    gap:12px;
    margin-top:22px;
  }
  .button{
    display:inline-flex;
    align-items:center;
    gap:8px;
    padding:11px 18px;
    text-decoration:none;
    border-radius:100px;
    font-size:0.95rem;
    font-weight:500;
    border:1px solid #E3DFD3;
    background:var(--cream);
    color:var(--navy);
    transition:transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease, background 0.2s ease;
  }
  .button:hover{ transform:translateY(-1px); border-color:var(--accent); background:#F1E2D6; }
  .button.primary{
    background:var(--navy);
    color:var(--cream);
    border-color:var(--navy);
  }
  .button.primary:hover{ background:var(--accent-text); border-color:var(--accent-text); color:#fff; }
  .button:focus-visible{ outline:2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset:2px; }
</style>
